+#### [invoice2data](https://github.com/invoice-x/invoice2data)
+> **Description:** invoice2data extracts structured fields from invoices using templates and OCR-compatible inputs. While not tax-specific, it is valuable for bookkeeping-adjacent tax workflows such as AP review, sales-tax support schedules, and invoice classification before reconciliation. The README focuses on pulling supplier names, invoice numbers, dates, amounts, and line-level details into machine-readable output. That makes it a practical tool for teams that need predictable field extraction without outsourcing sensitive billing documents. GitHub showed Python as primary and an MIT license.
