+> **Description:** LayoutParser provides a toolkit for document image analysis, especially for understanding page layouts and building custom document pipelines. Its README emphasizes layout detection, OCR workflow integration, and reusable tooling for document AI research and production. For tax professionals, this matters when page geometry itself carries meaning, such as forms, scanned notices, schedules, and statement packages where field position informs interpretation. GitHub showed Python as the primary language, an Apache-2.0 license, and a public repository still widely used for document analysis.
